(* FAST probe that disentangled the fp2 "var=Elem / error in update" failure.
 *
 * This is a VALID reversible program:  [fp_dyncond_bug]((nil . d)) = 'one
 * (for any non-nil d; 'two for d = nil), with the store cleared at the end.
 *
 * spec_av specializes it CORRECTLY:
 *   comp = [spec_av]((fp_dyncond_bug . ('S . nil)))
 *   [comp](d) evaluated DIRECTLY (data2program + evalProgram) = 'one / 'two.
 * So the residual is fine -- spec_av's dynamic-cond residualization is NOT the
 * culprit here.
 *
 * The failure appears ONLY when the (correct) comp is run through the ri.rwhile
 * self-interpreter (run_via_ri):  [comp](d) via ri raises "error in update".
 * The root cause is in ri.rwhile, not spec_av.  Two distinct ri.rwhile bugs:
 *   BUG 1 (FIXED via the CANON macro): 'cond cleared the saved entry-test value
 *     against the exit-assertion value by BIT-equality, but R-WHILE only needs
 *     equal TRUTHINESS (here entry `if D` value 'q vs assertion (=? R 'one)
 *     value (nil.nil)).  compare.rwhile etc. were unaffected (same predicate
 *     for test and assertion).
 *   BUG 2 (FIXED 2026-08-10; was the dominant one): the reversible self-clear
 *     `X ^= X` (this program's `D ^= D`) was mis-self-interpreted.  'ass did
 *     EVAL-EXP(E); DUPDATE(K); INV-EVAL-EXP(E); when E reads K the DUPDATE
 *     changes the store, so the re-reading INV-EVAL-EXP could not clear its
 *     temp -> "error in update".  Minimal isolations: `A ^= A`;
 *     `Y ^= 'k; Y ^= Y`.  FIX (examples/ri.rwhile, 'ass): the SAVED-VALUE
 *     method -- EVAL-EXP; save the value; INV-EVAL-EXP against the still
 *     UNCHANGED store; DUPDATE last; discard the saved copy.  Pinned by the
 *     `ri-selfclear` test group.
 *
 * Consequence, now closed: run_via_ri (the fp2 success criterion in
 * HANDOFF_fp2.md) used to fail on a CORRECT comp.  It agrees with
 * data2program+evalProgram on this program again.  The REAL fp2 spec_av bug is
 * a separate one, visible under direct eval too: the fp2 comp is incomplete
 * (leaves variables non-nil).
 *
 * See HANDOFF_fp2.md and memory second-futamura-projection-status. *)
read X;
  cons Sv D <= X;
  Sv ^= Sv;
  if D then R ^= 'one else R ^= 'two fi (=? R 'one);
  D ^= D;
write R
